<title>ITALY: Europa Metalli posts higher 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Europa Metalli posts higher 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Europa Metalli Spa, the Italian unit of the SMI group's KM Europa Metal AG, posted 1996 net profit of 20.3 billion lire, up from 12.4 billion in the June to December 1995 period.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the board proposed paying a dividend of 73 lire versus 44 lire.</p>
<p>As a result of group restructuring, SMI transferred Italian activities to KM Europa Metal from June 1, 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover in 1996 was 995.1 billion lire against 707 billion in the seven month 1995 period.</p>
<p>Net debt fell to 132 billion lire from 141 billion.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
